mixin () {
  /// Static Markdown documentation of this backend's public API.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Career Trials Backend API\n\nThis canister backs a bilingual (English / Vietnamese) career-orientation\nplatform for high-school students. It serves a public catalogue of career\ntrials, a public evidence portfolio, per-student enrolment tracking, and a\nshort multiple-choice knowledge test per trial whose submitted attempt is\nscored server-side and published automatically as an evidence card.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### `listTrials() : async [CareerTrial]` (query)\nReturns the full public career trial catalogue. Open to anonymous callers.\nEach entry carries `id`, `name`, `summary`, `tags` (skill/category labels),\n`daysToComplete`, and a `brief` with `description`, `checklist`, and\n`deliverables`. The catalogue is seeded with Marketing, Graphic Design,\nBusiness Analysis, Event Planning, Content Creation, and a \"Coming next\"\nplaceholder whose `daysToComplete` is `0` and whose brief is empty.\n\n### `getTrial(id : TrialId) : async ?CareerTrial` (query)\nReturns one trial by id, or `null` when no trial has that id. Open to\nanonymous callers.\n\n### `listEvidence() : async [EvidenceCard]` (query)\nReturns every public evidence card. Open to anonymous callers. Each card has\n`id`, `testerName`, `trialName`, `completionPercent` (0-100), `rating`\n(0-100), and `aspectScores`, a list of `{ aspect, score }` pairs where each\n`score` is 0-100. Six cards are seeded at install time; cards published by\n`submitTest` are appended to the same public list.\n\n### `listMyEnrollments() : async [EnrollmentView]` (query)\nReturns only the calling principal's own enrolments, each with the resolved\n`trialName`. Requires a signed-in caller: an anonymous caller receives an\nempty list. Ownership is derived from the caller's principal, never from an\nargument.\n\n### `listMyEvidence() : async [MyEvidenceCard]` (query)\nReturns only the calling principal's own evidence cards. Requires a signed-in\ncaller: an anonymous caller receives an empty list. A card is attributed to\nthe caller by the `testerName` stored on it, which is the display name the\ncaller set with `setMyDisplayName` (or the fallback `Student` when unset).\nEach card carries `id`, `trialId`, `trialName`, `completionPercent` (0-100),\n`rating` (0-100), and `aspectScores`. `trialId` identifies which trial the\ncard was published for, so the student area can join a card back to the\nenrolment it came from; it is resolved from the card's trial name against the\ncatalogue and is `0` when no catalogue trial has that name.\n\n### `getMyTestResult(trialId : TrialId) : async ?TestResult` (query)\nReturns the calling principal's own stored test result for one trial, or\n`null` when the caller has not tested that trial, the trial does not exist, or\nthe caller is anonymous. The result is derived from the caller's own\npublished evidence card for that trial — never from another student's data —\nand carries `trialId`, `trialName`, `score` (0-100), `completionPercent`\n(0-100), `aspectScores` (per-aspect 0-100 scores), and `evidenceId`. Because\n`submitTest` replaces a retake's card in place, this always returns the\ncaller's latest result for the trial. Ownership is derived from the caller's\nprincipal, never from an argument.\n\n### `enroll(trialId : TrialId) : async EnrollmentError` (update)\nEnrols the calling principal in a trial at 0% progress. Returns\n`#notSignedIn` for an anonymous caller, `#unknownTrial(id)` when no trial has\nthat id, and `#alreadyEnrolled(id)` when the caller already has an enrolment\nfor that trial. On success it returns `#ok(id)`, where `id` is the new\nenrolment id; `#ok` is the only success tag and every other variant is a\nfailure.\n\n### `updateProgress(enrollmentId : EnrollmentId, progressPercent : Nat) : async EnrollmentError` (update)\nUpdates the calling principal's own enrolment progress. Returns\n`#notSignedIn` for an anonymous caller, `#invalidProgress(n)` when `n` is\nabove 100, and `#notEnrolled(id)` when the caller has no enrolment with that\nid. On success it returns `#ok(id)` with the updated enrolment id; `#ok` is\nthe only success tag and every other variant is a failure. Progress is also\nset automatically by `submitTest` from the scored outcome.\n\n### `getMyProfile() : async ?StudentProfile` (query)\nReturns the calling principal's stored display name as\n`?{ displayName : Text }`, or `null` when the caller has never set one. Open\nto any caller; an anonymous caller always receives `null` because no profile\nis ever stored for an anonymous principal.\n\n### `setMyDisplayName(displayName : Text) : async ProfileError` (update)\nStores the calling principal's display name, which becomes the `testerName`\non every evidence card the caller publishes. The name is trimmed of leading\nand trailing whitespace before it is stored. Returns `#notSignedIn` for an\nanonymous caller and `#invalidName` when the trimmed name is empty or longer\nthan 60 characters. On success it returns `#ok`; `#ok` is the only success\ntag and every other variant is a failure. Calling it again replaces the\nstored name.\n\n### `getTrialTest(trialId : TrialId) : async ?TrialTestView` (query)\nReturns a trial's knowledge test as `?{ trialId, trialName, questions }`, or\n`null` when the trial does not exist or is not startable (the \"Coming next\"\nplaceholder, whose `daysToComplete` is `0`). Open to anonymous callers, but\nthe frontend prompts signed-out visitors to sign in before starting.\n\nEach question is a `TestQuestionView` with `id`, `prompt`, `options` (a list\nof `{ id, text }`), and `aspect` — the skill dimension the question scores.\nThe correct option is **never** included in this response; scoring happens\nonly in `submitTest`.\n\n### `submitTest(trialId : TrialId, answers : [TestAnswer]) : async TestError` (update)\nScores a submitted attempt server-side and publishes the result as an\nevidence card. `answers` is a list of `{ questionId, optionId }`; the student\nnever supplies a score. Returns:\n\n- `#notSignedIn` — the caller is anonymous.\n- `#unknownTrial(id)` — no trial has that id, or it has no test.\n- `#notEnrolled(id)` — the caller has no enrolment for that trial.\n- `#incomplete(ids)` — one or more questions were left unanswered; `ids`\n  lists the missing question ids.\n- `#invalidAnswer(questionId)` — an answer references a question that is not\n  part of this test, or an option that is not one of that question's options.\n- `#ok(result)` — the attempt was scored and published. `result` carries\n  `trialId`, `trialName`, `score` (0-100), `completionPercent` (0-100),\n  `aspectScores` (per-aspect 0-100 scores), and `evidenceId`.\n\n`#ok` is the only success tag and every other variant is a failure. The score\nis the percentage of correct answers; `completionPercent` equals the score;\neach aspect score is the percentage correct among the questions mapped to\nthat aspect. The caller's enrolment progress is set to the resulting\n`completionPercent`.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : async Text` (query)\nReturns this document as static Markdown. Open to anonymous callers. It reads\nno state, so its output never changes between calls.\n\n## OQL query surface\n\nThe canister also exposes the Caffeine Object Query Layer through the\n`caffeineai-oql` `Expose` mixin, which adds two controller-facing methods:\n\n- `schema() : async Text` — the JSON schema of every registered entity.\n- `execute(query : Text) : async Text` — runs a JSON query against them.\n\nThree entities are registered, each with its own authorization level:\n\n| Entity | Source | Authorization |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `careerTrial` | the public trial catalogue | public — anyone, including anonymous callers, reads all rows |\n| `evidenceCard` | the public evidence portfolio | public — anyone, including anonymous callers, reads all rows |\n| `enrollment` | per-student enrolments | controller-or-scoped — the controller reads all rows; a signed-in student reads only their own |\n\nThe `enrollment` entity flattens the per-student enrolment map into one row per\nenrolment and promotes the owning principal as an `owner` column. Its `trialId`\ncolumn is an edge into `careerTrial`, so a query can traverse\n`\"enrollment.trialId.name\"`. Because it is scoped, a signed-in caller sees only\nrows whose `owner` equals their own principal, and an anonymous caller sees\nnone.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- `listTrials`, `getTrial`, `listEvidence`, `getTrialTest`, and `getApiDoc`\n  are public and work for anonymous callers.\n- `listMyEnrollments`, `listMyEvidence`, `getMyTestResult`, `enroll`,\n  `updateProgress`, `getMyProfile`, `setMyDisplayName`, and `submitTest` act\n  on the caller's own records. They derive identity from the caller's\n  principal and never accept a principal as an argument, so one student\n  cannot read or modify another student's enrolments, profile, or results.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n  `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent that already\n  holds the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct\n  per-app principal against that origin (for example\n  `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with\n  the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration happens when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend.\n  A direct API caller can register by calling `_initialize_access_control`\n  once as a signed-in caller before any role-guarded call. The first\n  initializer receives the `#admin` role; every later caller receives `#user`.\n  An unregistered caller that reaches a role-guarded endpoint traps with\n  `User is not registered`, and an anonymous caller is treated as `#guest`.\n  A principal that never signed in through this app's frontend is unregistered\n  even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived\n  against a different origin is a different principal than the one the\n  frontend registered.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `TrialId`, `EvidenceId`, `EnrollmentId`, and every test `id` are `Nat`\n  identifiers.\n- `Timestamp` is `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`).\n- `score`, `completionPercent`, `rating`, and every `AspectScore.score` are\n  `Nat` on a 0-100 scale.\n- `tags`, `checklist`, `deliverables`, `aspectScores`, `questions`, `options`,\n  and `answers` are arrays; an empty array means \"none\", not \"unknown\".\n- `TestError` and `ProfileError` are variants: `#ok` is the only success tag.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\nAn enrolment moves from 0% to 100% through repeated `updateProgress` calls or\nthrough a `submitTest` outcome. There is no separate completion transition:\nreaching 100% is recorded but does not change the enrolment's state. Poll\n`listMyEnrollments()` after a mutation to read the authoritative progress and\n`updatedAt` value, and `listMyEvidence()`, `getMyTestResult(trialId)`, or\n`listEvidence()` to read a published card.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n`enroll` is not idempotent: a second call for the same trial returns\n`#alreadyEnrolled(id)` and creates nothing, so a retry after a timeout is\nsafe. `updateProgress` is idempotent for a given `(enrollmentId,\nprogressPercent)` pair — repeating it writes the same value and only advances\n`updatedAt`. `setMyDisplayName` is idempotent for the same name.\n\n`submitTest` is **not** idempotent in the sense of appending: the first\nsuccessful attempt for a `(student, trial)` pair creates a new evidence card,\nand every later attempt for the same pair **replaces that same card in place**\n— it never appends a duplicate. The returned `evidenceId` is the card's id, so\nretrying a submission overwrites the previous result rather than publishing a\nsecond card. No method deletes data; there is no destructive endpoint in this\nAPI.\n\n## Errors, traps, and limits\n\n- The enrolment, profile, and test methods return variant errors rather than\n  trapping on caller error.\n- `getTrial` and `getTrialTest` return `null` for an unknown or non-startable\n  trial; they do not trap.\n- The catalogue and the six seeded evidence cards are created at install time\n  and are read-only through this API.\n- The OQL query surface (`schema` and `execute`) exposes the `careerTrial` and\n  `evidenceCard` entities as public tables and the `enrollment` entity as a\n  controller-or-scoped table. A scoped caller that queries `enrollment` sees\n  only its own rows; the controller sees all rows.";
  };
};
